; SET-MAR and CLEAR-MAR over a range of words (sys/sys/qmisc.lisp,
; SI::MAP-MAR-PAGES): each page from the range's first word's to its last
; word's is visited once.  The old loops stepped #o200 words from the first
; word and stopped past the last: on the CADR's 256-word pages they missed
; the page holding the last word when that word lay in the page's first 127
; words and the step from the first word passed over it, depending on the
; first word modulo 128.  Here the range runs from 28 words below a page
; boundary to 50 words past it, so the old loop visited only the first page,
; and a write of the last word did not trap while its page was in core.
; Check a source change with
;   --compile --files sys/sys/qmisc.lisp,tools/system-check/lisp/mar-range.lisp
; The first two cases and the last are controls: a write of the first word
; traps, a write outside the range does not, and none once the MAR is
; cleared.  System 1003 without the change fails the third.
(progn (mar-set 100. 20.) (mar-trap-p 100.)) => T
(prog1 (mar-trap-p 130.) (si:clear-mar)) => NIL
(let ((low (- (mar-index (mar-page-after 100.)) 28.))) (mar-set low 79.) (prog1 (mar-trap-p (+ low 78.)) (si:clear-mar))) => T
(let ((low (- (mar-index (mar-page-after 100.)) 28.))) (mar-set low 79.) (si:clear-mar) (or (mar-trap-p low) (mar-trap-p (+ low 78.)))) => NIL
